gnals for snap supply disruption", "Global demand indicators for BD export exposure"], "runway": null, "verdict": "Brent consolidating at $94.11 — flat from yesterday's $6 crash, $17 below the $111 May peak. The decline is demand-driven, not supply normalization — signaling global slowdown risk alongside import-bill relief. Model $85–95 for H2."}, "verdict_tone": "bull", "summary_pills": [{"key": "BRENT", "tone": "neu", "value": "$94.11"}, {"key": "WTI", "tone": "neu", "value": "$90.55"}, {"key": "SPREAD", "tone": "neu", "value": "$3.56"}]}, {"id": "4614ddd1-7970-4674-ac67-d3514cf93b6b", "ord": 11, "news": [], "slug": "remit", "tldr": "Remittance at $3.13B; down 17% from record, trending toward mean.", "notes": [], "title": "Remittance", "series": [], "weight": 1, "metrics": [{"id": "235cff87-d743-44c1-bb8b-7bdfd8e52226", "ord": 0, "sub": "Down 17% from $3.76B record · reversion toward $2.89B mean", "tone": "warn", "delta": null, "label": "Monthly Remittance", "spark": null, "value": "$3.13B", "weight": 2, "changed": true, "delta_pct": null, "held_from": null, "next_print": null, "is_snapshot": false}], "verdict": "$3.13B monthly — reverting from $3.76B record toward mean.", "analysis": null, "brief_id": "bb0581b8-752f-4361-96c2-8a54b4718572", "freshness": "warming_up", "group_key": "markets", "banker_read": {"risk": ["Further reversion below $3B erases trade-gap offset", "Seasonal Eid spike may mask underlying trend decline"], "watch": ["May remittance print for reversion velocity", "Informal channel spread vs formal rate"], "runway": null, "verdict": "Monthly remittance at $3.13B — down 17% from the $3.76B record, reverting toward the $2.89B historical mean. Still above-mean but the trajectory is downward. Critical offset for the trade gap narrows if reversion continues."}, "verdict_tone": "warn", "summary_pills": [{"key": "MONTHLY", "tone": "warn", "value": "$3.13B"}, {"key": "VS RECORD", "tone": "warn", "value": "-17%"}]}, {"id": "d2953bcf-7847-46a0-a7ec-ffd9320